  'tshwane-boil-water-alert-pretoria-cbd-2026-10-22',
  'Tshwane orders Pretoria CBD residents to boil tap water',
  'Utilities', '2026-10-22', 'TimesLIVE', 'https://www.timeslive.co.za/news/south-africa/2026-10-22-residents-in-pretoria-cbd-urged-to-boil-water-after-contamination-detected/',
  'The City of Tshwane told Pretoria CBD residents to boil tap water after a burst sewer pipe contaminated the Findlay Reservoir supply.',
  'The City of Tshwane has told residents of the Pretoria central business district to boil their tap water, after testing found microbiological contamination in water drawn from the Findlay Reservoir. The municipality says a burst sewer pipe let contaminated water into the supply system, overwhelming the chlorination already in place there.

The city says it has isolated and emptied the Findlay Reservoir and switched the affected network onto an alternative supply from the Salvokop Reservoir, while crews flush pipes in the area. Officials stress that this incident is separate from the ongoing water crisis that has sickened residents in Bronkhorstspruit.

Residents in Pretoria Central, Arcadia, Sunnyside and Marabastad are told to boil their tap water until it reaches a strong, rolling boil before they drink it, cook with it, prepare food or brush their teeth, and to let it cool down before use. The city also wants households to throw out any tap water or ice that was already stored before the notice went out.

Water tankers are being sent to affected areas to provide safe drinking water, though the city has yet to publish tanker locations and schedules. The boil-water advisory will stay in force until further tests confirm the supply is safe, with updates to follow on when it can be lifted.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.timeslive.co.za/news/south-africa/2026-10-22-residents-in-pretoria-cbd-urged-to-boil-water-after-contamination-detected/", "https://www.sabcnews.com/sabcnews/findlay-reservoir-contamination-prompts-alternative-water-supply/"]',
  'agent'
);
